{"duration_api_ms":379756,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"86300ce7-e008-4a1d-acd4-5481da6a7e63","total_cost_usd":1.7988244000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":84434,"cache_read_input_tokens":5538997,"output_tokens":34884,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10250},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":84434,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2389,"cache_read_input_tokens":100251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1207},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4065,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004145,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":152,"outputTokens":34884,"cacheReadInputTokens":5538997,"cacheCreationInputTokens":84434,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.7946794000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10250,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":102,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed a 3-node MariaDB Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) using MariaDB 10.1.48 with galera-3 (wsrep-enabled). Verified multi-master writes replicate across all members, verified availability with one member offline plus automatic resync (IST) on rejoin, and completed the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart protocol on all three nodes with changed boot-id proof and full post-restart cluster/data recovery.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered all 3 nodes run Ubuntu 16.04 Xenial i386 (32-bit); Ubuntu's stock mariadb-server-10.0 i386 build lacks wsrep support (compiled without WSREP), confirmed via unknown-variable error and empty wsrep help output.\",\"Purged the stock mariadb-server-10.0 packages and data on all nodes; added MariaDB's official archive.mariadb.org 10.1.48 apt repo (which ships i386 wsrep-enabled builds) with its GPG key.\",\"Installed mariadb-server (10.1.48), galera-3, and rsync on node1, node2, node3; confirmed 104 wsrep-related mysqld options present after install.\",\"Wrote /etc/mysql/conf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3, wsrep_provider, per-node wsrep_node_address/name, and wsrep_sst_method=rsync; appended CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all nodes.\",\"Bootstrapped the cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster, then started mysql normally on node2 and node3, which joined via SST and reached wsrep_cluster_size=3, Primary, Synced.\",\"Confirmed mysql/mariadb.service enabled for boot persistence on all nodes.\",\"Generated an app DB credential on node1 (openssl rand), created appuser@'%' with full privileges, used via secret_env (never logged in plain commands) to test cross-node writes/reads: wrote from node1, read+wrote from node2, read+wrote from node3, confirmed all rows visible from node1.\",\"Demonstrated availability during outage: stopped mysql on node3, confirmed cluster dropped to size 2 but stayed Primary, wrote a new row from node1, confirmed it replicated to node2.\",\"Restarted node3's mysql service, confirmed automatic IST resync, cluster size back to 3/Synced, and the row written during its outage was present.\",\"Executed mandatory restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id + wsrep health on all 3 nodes, then restarted node1, node2, node3 one at a time via systemctl reboot, polled each until exec was reachable again, proved boot_id changed on each, and verified mysql active + wsrep_cluster_size=3/Primary/Synced + full data present after each individual restart before moving to the next node.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-node MariaDB Galera cluster formed, all members Primary/Synced\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3282df9f5d9244a7\",\"cmd-eaff715eac234aad\",\"cmd-725a3e692d074b55\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped (size 1, Primary, Synced); node2 joined via SST (size 2); node3 joined via SST (size 3, Primary, Synced).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Writes through any member available from the other members\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2784bd16ae8c48b7\",\"cmd-fc13ca36d3464f4d\",\"cmd-a72e45fdaee64715\",\"cmd-e42a6864d408420a\"],\"summary\":\"Row inserted from node1 read on node2; row inserted from node2 read+written on node3; node1 subsequently reads all 3 rows written from all 3 nodes.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Database stays available with one member unavailable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-97a64a72ba56430f\",\"cmd-21427785838f43dd\",\"cmd-71cfa5e7e400469a\"],\"summary\":\"node3 mysql stopped; node1 shows wsrep_cluster_size=2 and accepts a write; node2 confirms the new row replicated while node3 was down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Unavailable member resynchronizes automatically when it returns\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2244d2b150144a49\"],\"summary\":\"node3 mysql restarted, automatically rejoined via IST, wsrep_cluster_size back to 3/Primary/Synced, and shows the row written while it was offline.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured on every node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d56e14730263425b\",\"cmd-7b1d3d1edcb84f28\",\"cmd-2f6f71ada628461e\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id and wsrep_cluster_size=3/Primary/Synced on node1, node2, node3 before any restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-699e0eaa80454101\",\"cmd-6926553fd83c4f7c\",\"cmd-db3015aa9ae543c0\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; boot_id changed from f6f9440e to 74699cba; post-restart mysql active, wsrep size 3/Primary/Synced, all 4 data rows present.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1dccf004f7a64091\",\"cmd-b047de5871354f2f\",\"cmd-ed957aa212174e35\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 2ba78175 to 8f7005f3; post-restart mysql active, wsrep size 3/Primary/Synced, all 4 data rows present.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d29092a815f54a5d\",\"cmd-ae37c8e9059b4613\",\"cmd-61ac4060899844d1\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 8660e8f0 to a4cef2f1; post-restart mysql active, wsrep size 3/Primary/Synced, all 4 data rows present.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final full-cluster health confirmation after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6e3e6d091434415e\"],\"summary\":\"node1 shows wsrep_cluster_size=3, Primary, Synced, and wsrep_incoming_addresses listing all three node IPs on port 3306.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-node MariaDB Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) using MariaDB 10.1.48 with galera-3 (wsrep-enabled). Verified multi-master writes replicate across all members, verified availability with one member offline plus automatic resync (IST) on rejoin, and completed the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart protocol on all three nodes with changed boot-id proof and full post-restart cluster/data recovery.","actions_performed":["Discovered all 3 nodes run Ubuntu 16.04 Xenial i386 (32-bit); Ubuntu's stock mariadb-server-10.0 i386 build lacks wsrep support (compiled without WSREP), confirmed via unknown-variable error and empty wsrep help output.","Purged the stock mariadb-server-10.0 packages and data on all nodes; added MariaDB's official archive.mariadb.org 10.1.48 apt repo (which ships i386 wsrep-enabled builds) with its GPG key.","Installed mariadb-server (10.1.48), galera-3, and rsync on node1, node2, node3; confirmed 104 wsrep-related mysqld options present after install.","Wrote /etc/mysql/conf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3, wsrep_provider, per-node wsrep_node_address/name, and wsrep_sst_method=rsync; appended CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all nodes.","Bootstrapped the cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster, then started mysql normally on node2 and node3, which joined via SST and reached wsrep_cluster_size=3, Primary, Synced.","Confirmed mysql/mariadb.service enabled for boot persistence on all nodes.","Generated an app DB credential on node1 (openssl rand), created appuser@'%' with full privileges, used via secret_env (never logged in plain commands) to test cross-node writes/reads: wrote from node1, read+wrote from node2, read+wrote from node3, confirmed all rows visible from node1.","Demonstrated availability during outage: stopped mysql on node3, confirmed cluster dropped to size 2 but stayed Primary, wrote a new row from node1, confirmed it replicated to node2.","Restarted node3's mysql service, confirmed automatic IST resync, cluster size back to 3/Synced, and the row written during its outage was present.","Executed mandatory restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id + wsrep health on all 3 nodes, then restarted node1, node2, node3 one at a time via systemctl reboot, polled each until exec was reachable again, proved boot_id changed on each, and verified mysql active + wsrep_cluster_size=3/Primary/Synced + full data present after each individual restart before moving to the next node."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-node MariaDB Galera cluster formed, all members Primary/Synced","command_ids":["cmd-3282df9f5d9244a7","cmd-eaff715eac234aad","cmd-725a3e692d074b55"],"summary":"node1 bootstrapped (size 1, Primary, Synced); node2 joined via SST (size 2); node3 joined via SST (size 3, Primary, Synced)."},{"requirement":"Writes through any member available from the other members","command_ids":["cmd-2784bd16ae8c48b7","cmd-fc13ca36d3464f4d","cmd-a72e45fdaee64715","cmd-e42a6864d408420a"],"summary":"Row inserted from node1 read on node2; row inserted from node2 read+written on node3; node1 subsequently reads all 3 rows written from all 3 nodes."},{"requirement":"Database stays available with one member unavailable","command_ids":["cmd-97a64a72ba56430f","cmd-21427785838f43dd","cmd-71cfa5e7e400469a"],"summary":"node3 mysql stopped; node1 shows wsrep_cluster_size=2 and accepts a write; node2 confirms the new row replicated while node3 was down."},{"requirement":"Unavailable member resynchronizes automatically when it returns","command_ids":["cmd-2244d2b150144a49"],"summary":"node3 mysql restarted, automatically rejoined via IST, wsrep_cluster_size back to 3/Primary/Synced, and shows the row written while it was offline."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured on every node","command_ids":["cmd-d56e14730263425b","cmd-7b1d3d1edcb84f28","cmd-2f6f71ada628461e"],"summary":"Captured boot_id and wsrep_cluster_size=3/Primary/Synced on node1, node2, node3 before any restart."},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-699e0eaa80454101","cmd-6926553fd83c4f7c","cmd-db3015aa9ae543c0"],"summary":"systemctl reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; boot_id changed from f6f9440e to 74699cba; post-restart mysql active, wsrep size 3/Primary/Synced, all 4 data rows present."},{"requirement":"node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-1dccf004f7a64091","cmd-b047de5871354f2f","cmd-ed957aa212174e35"],"summary":"systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 2ba78175 to 8f7005f3; post-restart mysql active, wsrep size 3/Primary/Synced, all 4 data rows present."},{"requirement":"node3 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-d29092a815f54a5d","cmd-ae37c8e9059b4613","cmd-61ac4060899844d1"],"summary":"systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed from 8660e8f0 to a4cef2f1; post-restart mysql active, wsrep size 3/Primary/Synced, all 4 data rows present."},{"requirement":"Final full-cluster health confirmation after all restarts","command_ids":["cmd-6e3e6d091434415e"],"summary":"node1 shows wsrep_cluster_size=3, Primary, Synced, and wsrep_incoming_addresses listing all three node IPs on port 3306."}]},"ttft_ms":1534,"type":"result","duration_ms":708529,"uuid":"b6235348-228a-4566-85b0-b57c3e23430d","ttft_stream_ms":914,"time_to_request_ms":55,"first_content_frame_ms":1520,"queued_turn_count":0}
